meta {
  name: Generate upload authorization
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/media/upload-signature?target={{target}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  target: {{target}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    for (const key of ["uploadUrl", "fileUrl", "publicId"]) {
      if (res.body?.[key]) bru.setVar(key, res.body[key]);
    }
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  # Generate upload authorization

  `GET /api/media/upload-signature`

  Generate a SAS URL for a direct Azure Blob upload.

  ## Authentication

  Admin or Editor; inherited Bearer token.

  ## Parameters

  | Name | Location | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | target | Query | Example: `{{target}}`. |

  ## Request body

  No request body.

  ## Response

  HTTP **200**.

  ```json
  {
    "uploadUrl": "https://example.blob.core.windows.net/archive-media/photos/uuid?sv=...&sig=...",
    "fileUrl": "https://example.blob.core.windows.net/archive-media/photos/uuid",
    "publicId": "archive-media/photos/uuid",
    "provider": "AzureBlob"
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  - 400: missing/blank target.
  - 500: unhandled storage configuration or Azure failure.
  - 401: missing, invalid, or expired Bearer token.
  - 403: authenticated token with an insufficient role.

  Automatic model validation can return ValidationProblemDetails; explicit controller errors use a message field. Authentication middleware errors may have no body.

  ## Notes

  target is required: use container/folder, for example archive-media/photos, archive-media/videos, or gallery-media/articles. SAS allows create/write and expires 15 minutes after generation. Upload bytes with PUT to uploadUrl using x-ms-blob-type: BlockBlob and the file Content-Type; authorize that request with the SAS rather than the API JWT. Then register fileUrl/publicId via Create post or Add assets. The script captures uploadUrl, fileUrl, and publicId in runtime variables.

  Examples contain fictitious data. The assertion checks the successful scenario; a missing record or insufficient permissions can produce a different documented status.
}
